@bank all
// SW6 (ending writer A), the friends (ending spec, "The news gets out", Friday Day 33 until Saturday 20:00, and the
// call home; section 9: content/ending/friends.lines). The close friends' own scenes are meetings beside this file:
// endingFriend.pell | .tomas | .kovac-zainab | .bramwell-basil | .halloran-emeka | .rina; Zeke's are endingZekeFriday
// and endingZekeSunday.stay | .go. These lines are for everyone else at the friend tiers, the chat card's button, the
// news going round, and what friends say once you've answered and once it's settled.
// FLAGS (agreed with lead 39 / EN1): end.offer; end.now.<stay|go|unsure>; end.stay / end.go (settled at the address).

// ---- the chat card's button (a friend's card, Friday Day 33 until her address) and its use
== ending.ui.friend.button
- About the transfer

// ---- a friend's own take, on their card (90 at most), for friends without their own scene. Some say stay, some say
// go, some won't say. The engine picks one per person, so each friend gets their own.
== ending.friend.talk
? tier>=friend
- Headquarters! {wow}. I'd go. I mean, I'd miss you. But I'd go.   #warm
- Stay. Sorry. You asked. Stay. The Wren's better with you on her.   #warm
- I won't say. Whatever I say, you'll hear the other one louder. That's how it works.
- You did in four weeks what takes most people a year. They noticed. Course they did.   #warm
- Go and see what it's like. You can always come back out. People do.
- I'd stay. But I've never wanted a desk in my life. You might. That's allowed.
- My gut says stay. My head says go. My stomach says it's nearly dinner.   #funny
- Big choice. Don't make it hungry. Don't make it tired. Then make it.
- Whatever you pick, I'll be on the right side of it. Which is your side.   #warm
? tier>=close
- I don't want you to go. There. That's selfish and true. Now forget I said it and choose.   #warm
- You'd be brilliant there. You'd be brilliant here. That's the trouble with you.   #warm
- If you go, write. If you stay, I'll stop pretending I wasn't worried.   #warm
? dept:works tier>=friend
- Works without you? The board'd notice. The board notices everything.   #funny
- Calder's been quiet all day. Quieter. You know what that means.
? dept:galley tier>=friend
- Brennan's put your favourite on for Sunday. Just in case. Don't tell her I told you.   #warm
? dept:watch tier>=friend
- The Watch knew before you did. We're sorry. It's the lift. It hears everything.   #funny
? dept:survey tier>=friend
- Our charts go to headquarters to be read. Go and read them. Or stay and make them.

// ---- Zeke on his card, before his Friday evening talk (he wants it at the tea corner, after dinner)
== ending.friend.talk.torres-zeke
? !flag:end.zeke.friday
- Not here. Not with coil three listening. After dinner, tea corner. I'll find you.
?
- I said what I had to say. The rest's yours. I'm here, though.   #warm

// ---- the news going round, Friday and Saturday (bubbles, 60 at most; anyone who knows you)
== ending.rumour
- Did you hear? Headquarters wants the new hand.
- Headquarters asked for {me}. By name, someone said.
- Is it true about the transfer? Everyone's asking.
- The Captain had the new hand up to the ready room. Big news.
- They'll be at headquarters by next week. Or not. Who knows?
? dept:works
- Works might be losing one. Calder hasn't said a word.
? place:mess
- Brennan's heard. Brennan always hears first.   #funny

// ---- after you've told the Captain, before her address (chat card lines, 90 at most). It isn't settled yet: they
// speak of it as what you've said, not what will happen.
== ending.friend.told
? flag:end.now.stay tier>=friend
- You told her you're staying? I heard. I'm trying very hard not to celebrate yet.   #warm
- Staying, they say. Good. I hadn't packed you a goodbye. I'm terrible at those.   #funny
- You're staying? Don't change your mind. Unless you want to. But don't.   #funny
? flag:end.now.go tier>=friend
- You told her yes. Headquarters. I'm happy for you. Give me a day to look happy.   #warm
- Going, then. I knew you'd be brilliant somewhere bigger. I just liked you here.   #warm
- You said yes? Good. Proper good. I'm not crying. That's the scrubber dust.   #funny
? flag:end.now.unsure tier>=friend
- Still thinking? Good. Anyone who's sure about that is lying.
- Not sure yet? The Captain'll ask you on Sunday, in front of everyone. No pressure.   #funny

// ---- settled at the address (Sunday, from about 15:00). Stay lasts until Monday's first morning (Writer B's endgame
// pool takes over then). Go lasts until the ramp.
== ending.friend.settled
? flag:end.stay
- You're staying! Good. Right. That's that, then. Good.   #warm
- I heard the Captain's speech. "We're keeping them." I'm keeping that line.   #warm
- Staying. Excellent. I owe Halloran a scone. Long story.   #funny
- You're staying, so you can help with the board on Monday. Welcome back. You never went.   #funny
? flag:end.go
- Tomorrow, then. I'll be in the bay. Half nine. I won't be late.   #warm
- Headquarters. Look at you. Write to us. Real letters.   #warm
- I don't like goodbyes. I'll do this one properly anyway.   #warm
- You'll be back out here one day. They always come back to the frontier.
? flag:end.go tier>=close
- I'm not saying goodbye today. Tomorrow. One at a time.   #warm

// ---- the call home about the transfer (the booths' option "Call home about the transfer", level 2, once, Thursday
// 16:30 to Saturday). One-sided, as every call home since 0.62.0: Mum on the line (she/her; calls you "chick"), with
// Gran in the room. Proud, and careful not to choose for you. In order, 8 lines (moment lines, 140 at most).
// Canon: Mum drives the number nine bus and does pottery; Gran has the allotment and the box ("Is the light on?").
== ending.call.mum.1
- Chick! Your letter came. I read it twice. Then I read it to Gran. Then she read it to me.   #warm
== ending.call.mum.2
- Headquarters. Headquarters! I told the whole number nine bus. A man in the back clapped.   #funny
== ending.call.mum.3
- Now listen. I'm not going to tell you what to do. I've promised Gran. She's watching me.   #warm
== ending.call.mum.4
- When you went out there, I cried at the port for an hour. I'd do it again tomorrow.   #warm
== ending.call.mum.5
- Gran says: "The allotment says go." I don't know what that means. Nor does she.   #funny
== ending.call.mum.6
- Jo says whatever you pick is right, because you picked it. Steve the stapler agrees.   #funny
== ending.call.mum.7
- Your shelf's still here. It'll be here either way. That's all I wanted to say, really.   #warm
== ending.call.mum.8
- We're proud of you, chick. Here, there, anywhere. Love to you. Gran says love too.   #warm
== ending.ui.booth.option
- Call home about the transfer
